-----Original Message-----
From: Sofie Peeters <s.peeters@corp-europe.example>
Sent: Monday, 05 October 2026 08:40
To: Marta Kowalska
Subject: RE: Missing ADR documents UN 1263 - Antwerp

The DGDs existed in SAP but were never printed, because the print job went to=
 the wrong printer in the office. The gate only checks the driver ID and the =
delivery number, so a gate check would not help much. I would rather put the =
check with the dispatcher before loading starts. Nobody loads a pallet of UN =
1263 until the dispatcher has the printed and signed DGD in hand. That is ear=
lier than the gate and also avoids reloading a truck that cannot leave.

Kind regards,
Sofie Peeters
Warehouse supervisor Antwerp
